     "q": "How do `try` and `except` work?",
     "a": "Code that might fail goes in `try:`. If an exception is raised, Python jumps to the first matching `except` block. Unhandled exceptions stop the program with a traceback.",
     "e": "Catch the most specific exception you can handle meaningfully.",
