     "q": "What do `else` and `finally` do in a `try` statement?",
     "a": "`else` runs only if no exception occurred, so keep the \"happy path\" there. `finally` always runs, with or without an exception, and is used for cleanup.",
     "e": "Putting the success code in `else` avoids accidentally catching exceptions raised by it.",
