     "level": "B",
     "q": "What is NumPy, and why is it faster than Python lists?",
     "a": "NumPy provides `ndarray`, a typed, contiguous array with operations implemented in C. Vectorised operations (`arr * 2`) run over the whole array without Python-level loops, often 10 to 100 times faster.",
