     "q": "How do you filter rows in pandas?",
     "a": "With a boolean mask: `df[df[\"sales\"] > 100]`. Combine conditions with `&` and `|`, and put each condition in parentheses. `df.query(\"sales > 100 and region == 'EU'\")` is a readable alternative; `.isin([...])` checks membership.",
     "e": "Use `&`/`|` rather than `and`/`or` on Series; the keywords raise \"truth value is ambiguous\".",
     "code": "import pandas as pd\ndf = pd.DataFrame({\"region\": [\"EU\", \"US\", \"EU\", \"APAC\"], \"sales\": [120, 340, 90, 200]})\nprint(df[(df[\"sales\"] > 100) & (df[\"region\"] != \"US\")])\nprint(df.query(\"sales < 150\"))",
